This is a 42 School project on Docker running the following containers:
-- MariaDB
-- Wordpress
-- Static HTML
-- Nginx server
-- Adminer (->MariaDB)

This set up:
The HAZARDOUS PROJECT (static html)		at :hazardous.fr
A Wordpress dynamic website 			at :npolack.42.fr
Adminer to manage MariaDB database		at :admin.npolack.42.fr

To run on MacOs using colima:

	brew install colima

1) To give colima write permissions on volumes, use:

	colima start --edit
	then add to configuration file:

	#MacOs user uid & gid (id -u && id -g)
	guest:
	  uid: 501
	  gid: 20

	mounts:
	  - location: "/path/to/volumes"
	  writable: true
	
	colima stop
	colima delete
	colima start

2) if any problems "error getting credential" delete the lines: "credsStore": "desktop" in .docker/config.json

	{
	  "auths": {},
	  "credsStore": "desktop", <-- line to delete
	  "currentContext": "colima"
	}

